{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong baseline using the most principled full-pipeline configuration. I select config_020 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, concat fusion) because: (1) multimodal is the core hypothesis of this study and is expected to outperform unimodal baselines; (2) multiprofile with transformer aggregation is the most expressive way to capture inter-profile relationships; (3) scgpt provides learned, biologically-informed RNA representations superior to linear PCA; (4) imagenet_vit_l is the strongest available image encoder. This experiment tests whether the full 'best-of-each-component' pipeline achieves high validation accuracy, giving me a reference point. Subsequent experiments can then ablate individual choices (e.g., swap to resnet50, avgpool, or concat vs. weighted) to identify which components drive performance. Expected relative cost: high (~75-85% of maximum), driven by the ViT-Large image encoder, transformer aggregation over multiple profiles, and scgpt fine-tuning. Accepting this cost upfront is justified because it is the configuration most likely to be near-optimal, and establishing a strong ceiling early allows efficient exploitation in the remaining 9 experiments."
}

